# C# raw string literals keep the source's line endings verbatim (C# 11 does not
# normalize them), and the code builds text with explicit "\n". A CRLF checkout on
# the Windows runners would therefore turn every multi-line expected value into
# "\r\n" and every layout assertion would fail. Store and check out LF so a run is
# the same on Windows and on the macOS/Linux hosts.
*.cs    text eol=lf
*.csproj text eol=lf
*.props text eol=lf
*.targets text eol=lf
*.sln   text eol=lf
*.xaml  text eol=lf
*.ps1   text eol=lf
